agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** Read-path sanitization (`redactSecretsInPayload`, `stripVaultPaths`, and `sanitizeToolOutput`) is on the critical security path for bootstrap/search/get responses, yet the test suite has zero coverage proving secrets are redacted and vault paths are stripped on output. A regression would silently re-expose credentials stored before write-time detection improved.

**Correção sugerida:**

```ts
import { sanitizeToolOutput, redactSecretsInPayload, stripVaultPaths } from './safety.js';

it('sanitizeToolOutput redacts secrets and strips vault paths', () => {
  const token = 'ghp_' + 'a'.repeat(36);
  const out = sanitizeToolOutput({
    path: '/home/user/.spec-memo/projects/p/traps/t.md',
    body: `token=${token}`
  }) as { path?: string; body: string };
  assert.equal(out.path, undefined);
  assert.match(out.body, /\[REDACTED:GitHub Personal Access Token\]/);
  assert.doesNotMatch(out.body, /ghp_/);
});
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 6/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: `sanitizeToolOutput` defined at line 158; repo-wide grep shows usage in `tools.ts` and `adapter.ts` but no tests; `safety.test.ts` covers write-time `assertNoSecrets` only. 2. Scenario: future edit removes or narrows `redactSecretsInPayload` → MCP bootstrap returns an older vault record containing a GitHub token → agent context leaks credential. 3. Protection: write-time blocking tests exist; no read-path contract test locks the fail-closed behavior required by PRODUCT.PRD. 4. Discards: not asking for 100% coverage—this targets a security invariant with no automated guard.

**Caminhos analisados:** /src/safety.ts, /src/safety.test.ts, /src/tools.test.ts, /src/adapter.test.ts
</details>
